From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 15:40:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] glm5_next/cuda: TF_GLM_DENSE=q4 on the AFD attention node
 (MiaAI-Lab recipe patches 0002, 0005, 0013, 0028)

Ports Mia's AI Lab's (@MiaAI-Lab) 4-bit dense weights from the GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Sparks recipe
(github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold @ cf28cc4, v1.4; Apache License 2.0, Copyright
2026 MiaAI-Lab) onto the split's world-1 attention node:

- 0005-glm-dense-q4: quantize4_mse (MSE-searched affine 4-bit groups of 64, bf16 scale and bias), make_dense_q4,
  stack_dense_q4, q4_weights (the startup estimate);
- 0013-glm-decode-rounds: quantize4_mse_raw (the untiled MLX layout, split out, math unchanged) and no per-head
  kv_k / kv_v copies beside the latent path's absorb (kv_b stays BF16 behind it);
- 0002-glm-dense-fp8: F8 / make_f8 / _fmm / _matmul_f8 / fp8_weights, the head's format under q4 (TF_GLM_DENSE=fp8
  itself is not ported);
- 0028-glm-lean-prompt-scratch: prompt_split_k (4-bit prompt projections keep no split-K partials).

The quantizers are copied op for op, so the world-1 node's codes and scales are the recipe's two TP2 ranks' bytes
from the same checkpoint, joined by the split rule (rows quantize independently, and a column half is whole groups
of 64). The estimate reads cfg.quant only under q4, so upstream's capacity tests, whose configs carry no quant, run
as before.

Default unchanged: TF_GLM_DENSE unset or bf16 builds the same objects as before (kv_k / kv_v included). No CUDA or
C++ source changes: the 4-bit matmuls are TensorFold's tensorfold_qmm_v5 extension, the FP8 head a Triton kernel.

Tests: tests/test_glm_q4dense.py (CPU: flag-off bytes against tests/data/glm_q4dense_base_digests.json, the recipe's
copies, TP2 vs world 1; with TF_Q4_FIXTURES, real checkpoint tensors against the recipe tree's own per-rank bytes in
tests/data/glm_q4dense_mia_digests.json).

Credit: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the ported code's headers name MiaAI-Lab and the patches.

Co-authored-by: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
